# Git workflow

`main` is the release branch. Do not commit on it, and do not push it.

`dev` is `main` plus updates that are not released yet. Before starting work, fetch and merge `origin/main` into `dev`.

Do each change in a worktree branched from `dev`. Open a pull request into `dev`. A release is a pull request from `dev` into `main`.

```bash
git fetch origin
git switch dev && git merge origin/main
git worktree add ../argus-curator-<topic> -b <topic> dev
```

Do not force-push `main`. Do not commit secrets.
